==Old English==

===Etymology===
''Tiwes'' (''genitive'' of [[Tiw|Tīw]]) + [[dæg|dæġ]] (corresponding to {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*Tīwas dagaz}}). Cognate with Old Frisian ''Tiesdei'', Old High German ''zīostag'' (dialectal German ''Zistig''), Old Norse ''týrsdagr'' (Swedish ''[[tisdag]]''). Used in translation of the Latin ''[[dies Martis]]''

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtiwezdæj/|lang=ang}}

